WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.138
What is a day trade?

2
00:00:01.258 --> 00:00:04.973
Opening and closing a position during the same trading day.

3
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.114
A same-day example.

4
00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:09.184
Buy at 10 a.m. Monday.

5
00:00:09.304 --> 00:00:11.278
Sell at 2 p.m. Monday.

6
00:00:11.398 --> 00:00:12.710
That is a day trade.

7
00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:14.899
A different-day example.

8
00:00:15.019 --> 00:00:17.108
Buy on Monday and sell on Friday.

9
00:00:17.228 --> 00:00:18.935
This is not a same-day trade.

10
00:00:19.458 --> 00:00:20.712
Speed brings risk.

11
00:00:20.832 --> 00:00:24.431
Fast price movements can create losses quickly.

12
00:00:24.551 --> 00:00:27.024
Frequent trades do not guarantee income.

13
00:00:27.544 --> 00:00:28.926
Learn before you trade.

14
00:00:29.046 --> 00:00:33.620
Sprout runs simulated prices 24/7.

15
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:40.056
Real US regular sessions generally run 9:30 a.m.–4 p.m. Eastern on trading days.

